# Cisco Networking Lab: Router R2 and VLAN 10 Configuration

**Date:** October 12, 2026  
** Device: ** Cisco Router R2  
**Technologies:** Cisco IOS, IPv4, VLANs, 802.1Q, Router-on-a-Stick

## Overview

This lab documents the configuration of Cisco Router R2, including interface addressing and a subinterface for VLAN 10. The goal is to establish connectivity between routers and configure inter-VLAN routing using 802.1Q encapsulation.

## 1. Basic Router Configuration

### Objectives
- Set the router hostname to R2.
- Configure the FastEthernet0/0 interface.
- Enable the physical interfaces.
- Prepare FastEthernet0/1 for VLAN subinterfaces.

### Configuration

```cisco
Router> enable
Router# configure terminal
Router(config)# hostname R2

R2(config)# interface FastEthernet0/0
R2(config-if)# ip address 10.0.0.2 255.255.255.252
R2(config-if)# no shutdown
R2(config-if)# exit

R2(config)# interface FastEthernet0/1
R2(config-if)# no shutdown
R2(config-if)# exit
```

## 2. VLAN 10 Subinterface Configuration

### Objectives
- Create a subinterface on FastEthernet0/1.
- Configure 802.1Q encapsulation for VLAN 10.
- Assign the VLAN 10 gateway IP address.

### Configuration

```cisco
R2(config)# interface FastEthernet0/1.10
R2(config-subif)# encapsulation dot1Q 10
R2(config-subif)# ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.192
R2(config-subif)# no shutdown
R2(config-subif)# exit

R2(config)# end
R2# copy running-config startup-config
```

## 3. IP Addressing Table

| Interface | IP Address | Subnet Mask | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| FastEthernet0/0 | 10.0.0.2 | 255.255.255.252 | Router-to-router link |
| FastEthernet0/1 | No IP assigned | — | Physical trunk interface |
| FastEthernet0/1.10 | 192.168.10.1 | 255.255.255.192 | VLAN 10 default gateway |

## 4. VLAN 10 Network Details

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| VLAN ID | 10 |
| Network address | 192.168.10.0/26 |
| Default gateway | 192.168.10.1 |
| Usable host range | 192.168.10.1–192.168.10.62 |
| Broadcast address | 192.168.10.63 |
| Encapsulation | IEEE 802.1Q |

## 5. Verification

Use the following commands to verify the router configuration.

```cisco
show ip interface brief
show running-config
show interfaces FastEthernet0/1.10
show ip route
```

### Verification Checklist

- [ ] Verify FastEthernet0/0 has the correct IP address.
- [ ] Confirm FastEthernet0/1 is enabled.
- [ ] Confirm FastEthernet0/1.10 uses VLAN 10 encapsulation.
- [ ] Verify the VLAN 10 gateway address is configured.
- [ ] Test connectivity between a VLAN 10 client and its default gateway.
- [ ] Save the running configuration.

