## 7. Important Notes

- FastEthernet0/1 must connect to a switch port configured as an 802.1Q trunk that carries VLAN 10.
- The VLAN must exist on the connected switch, and the client-facing switch ports must be assigned to VLAN 10.
- FastEthernet0/1 does not need an IP address for this router-on-a-stick configuration because the IP address is assigned to the subinterface.
- The router-to-router link uses the `10.0.0.0/30` network. The other endpoint should use `10.0.0.1/30`.

